# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every rule in this file says WHY. A rule without a reason is one nobody dares
# remove, and this project's ignores carry real decisions — licensing, machine
# specificity, generated-vs-source — that are not recoverable from the path.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies and editor/tooling state.
node_modules
.env
/.idea/
.claude/

# Unminified dev bundles built by `npm run dev` / `npm run browser-watch`.
# The published bundles in build/ and browser/ ARE committed.
/dev/
/browser-dev/

# Scratch test and timing directories predating the __tests__/ and bench/
# layouts. Local only; nothing references them.
/tests/
speed_tests/

# `npm pack` output.
*.tgz

# Stray file created by an editor mangling a CSS @charset rule.
@charset

# Per-project agent instructions — local working notes, not project source.
CLAUDE.md


# Large ephemeral outputs from bench/jit_inspection.js
/bench/jit_asm_dump.txt
/bench/jit_asm_core_dump.txt
/bench/turbo-*.json
/jit_trace.txt
/jit_asm.txt

# Vendored lcms2 C source (downloaded by bench/lcms_c/fetch-lcms2.sh).
# We commit the bench glue (bench_lcms.c / Makefile / README / fetch
# scripts) but NOT the third-party lcms2 source tree — too big, has
# its own upstream.
/bench/lcms_c/lcms2-2.18/
/bench/lcms_c/lcms2-2.19/
/bench/lcms_c/lcms2-*/
/bench/lcms_c/*.o
/bench/lcms_c/bench_lcms
/bench/lcms_c/bench_lcms.exe
/bench/lcms_c/bench_content_matrix
/bench/lcms_c/bench_content_matrix.exe

# lcms_compat/ harness — profiles are licensed artefacts (Adobe,
# IDEAlliance, ECI, RISO, etc.) so user-supplied copies stay local.
# See bench/lcms_compat/profiles/README.md for the licensing split.
/bench/lcms_compat/profiles/*
!/bench/lcms_compat/profiles/README.md

# The reference .it8 set was committed until 1.5.5 — 150 files, 63 MB of
# measurements derived from those profiles. Untracked now mainly because
# nobody needs OUR copy: derived measurement data is what anyone with the same
# profiles and the same lcms version computes for themselves. Derived data is
# a grey area rather than a real concern, so this is caution plus 63 MB, not a
# licensing retreat. Same treatment as testbed/testData/ below.
#
# PROFILES are the actual line. Nothing that a vendor licenses gets committed.
/bench/lcms_compat/reference/*
!/bench/lcms_compat/reference/README.md

# Scratch / work-in-progress instrumented lcms2 tree — will be
# distilled down to a patch file under bench/lcms_compat/lcms_patch/
# in v1.5 (deferred from v1.3 to keep the release scoped), at which
# point this whole folder goes away.
/bench/lcms_exposed/

# Private work-in-progress — not ready for public repo
/_wip/
/__wip/
.cursor/

# Old browser bundles, pulled by `npm run archive` — build artefacts, not source.
bench/archive/

# Superseded one-off benches and the large ephemeral asm dumps. Kept locally
# because they are occasionally worth re-reading, out of the repo because
# nothing references them and two of them are 16 MB of generated text.
bench/_archive/

# Decoded photo corpus — ~27 MB of derived .rgb.bin/.cmyk.bin planes.
# The SOURCE images in bench/release_matrix/images/ ARE committed (Unsplash
# licence, see their CREDITS.md) so the published comparison is reproducible;
# only the generated planes are ignored. Rebuild them with:
#   node bench/release_matrix/make_corpus.cjs
bench/release_matrix/corpus/
bench/release_matrix/node_modules/

# Reproduction runs from bench/reproduce.js — raw timing output, machine-specific,
# superseded by the next run. Curated summaries (bench/results/v1.5.0-dev.md)
# stay tracked, as do the loose logs' curated equivalents.
#
# Two sibling trees are deliberately NOT ignored, because a control that lives
# on one disk is not a control:
#
#   bench/baseline/<machine>/            the pinned reference every refactor is
#                                        gated against (scripts/bench_compare.js).
#                                        Per machine: a Ryzen pin is not a
#                                        control for an M2.
#   bench/history/<version>/<machine>/   frozen per-release measurements, so a
#                                        figure published in 1.5.5 can still be
#                                        re-derived in 1.9.
#
# ~120 KB each. See bench/baseline/README.md.
bench/results/[0-9]*/

# Licensed ICC profiles — same rule as bench/lcms_compat/profiles/ above.
# testbed/profiles/README.md says so of itself: ICC profiles are licensed
# artefacts and most of what ships in a real prepress workflow cannot be
# redistributed on a public repo. Supply your own licensed copies locally.
# The READMEs that say WHICH profiles the harness expects stay tracked.
/testbed/profiles/*
!/testbed/profiles/README.md

# Reference .it8 measurements, derived by running lcms against the profiles.
# Grey area rather than a real concern — kept out because nobody needs our
# copy, not because it could not be shared. Generate them locally.
/testbed/testData/

# One six-colour customer press profile lived in testbed/profiles/6col/ and was
# tracked before the profiles rule existed. Untracked in 1.6; the /testbed/
# profiles rule above already covers the directory, this is just a note that
# the file is still on disk and is deliberately not coming back.
#
# What IS still tracked, deliberately:
#   __tests__/*.icc          the test pair — publicly redistributable
#   samples/profiles/*.icc   sRGB2014 (ICC.org) and the ECI set, all published
#                            as free downloads by their own publishers
#   testbed/profiles/devicelink/, lcms_testbed/
#                            synthetic — generated by the test code and by
#                            lcms's own testbed, no third-party IP at all

# Loose reproduce/pool logs and one-off dumps beside the timestamped runs.
/bench/results/*.log
/bench/results/multicore_matrix*.json
/bench/results/multicore_scaling*.json
